{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 6, :comments ["<b>And behold, a youth crying.</b> For he appeared like a grown youth, and this crying was on account of ״עִמּוֹ אָנֹכִי בְצָרָה״ (Psalms 91:15), as it is written ״כִּי יָדַעְתִּי אֶת מַכְאֹבָיו״ (Exodus 3:7) — that is to say, I feel his pain as it were, and this is the reduplication of ״אֶהְיֶה אֲשֶׁר אֶהְיֶה״ (Exodus 3:14), for in their distress He too is distressed. And some say that for this reason his voice was heard like a youth's, so that Pharaoh's daughter would think that he had been born long ago, for if not so she would not save him from doubt — for perhaps he is the redeemer and was born on that very day that the astrologers had spoken of."], :book :exodus, :voice :kli-yakar, :lang :en, :chapter 2, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:17:51.942006838Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}